From d2176cf86fe5769c331dcf56c92a50d439b96f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 17:59:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00836/11171] [outer-loop] #4 v4 DECISIVE: energy TEACHES
 (+1.1%, 3/3 seeds) and BEATS gold-SFT; line RETIRED

3 seeds, n_eval=2000 (SE ~0.5%). Both energy generative modes decisively positive:
in-loop gate +2.2% (3/3 tight), energy-as-teacher +1.1% (3/3, ~2 SE/seed) -- and
energy-RFT BEAT the gold-SFT control (-0.4%). Verifier-only self-certified RFT is
on-distribution/learnable and out-teaches raw labels on an under-trained base =
direct evidence for verifier-as-self-improvement-reward (Phase-3 thesis).

REVISED line conclusion (RETIRED): 'energy verifies, doesn't generate' was too
strong. Energy's DECISIVE value is verification (moat+panel), but it adds real,
modest, HEADROOM-gated generative value via (a) in-loop gate and (b) RFT teacher
(beats labels w/ headroom). Naive descent (0.000) + rerank (hurts) fail. Headroom
law unifies (same as P0.1). Headline strengthened: Carnot is the verifier -- and the
verifier can bootstrap a generator. Forward hook: scale from Sudoku proxy to
ensemble-on-reasoning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
